# Reverse proxy + automatic TLS (Let's Encrypt) in front of `backend`.
#
# BACKEND_DOMAIN comes from .env — Caddy substitutes {$VAR} at startup.
# Caddy always terminates TLS on its container's port 443 (and does the
# ACME HTTP-01 challenge on its container's port 80); which HOST ports
# those map to is controlled separately by CADDY_HTTP_PORT/CADDY_HTTPS_PORT
# in docker-compose.yml. If you map the host HTTPS port to anything other
# than 443, Let's Encrypt's HTTP-01/TLS-ALPN-01 challenges will fail
# (they only ever probe the domain on 80/443) — switch to a DNS-01
# challenge (see Caddy docs for your DNS provider's module) if you need a
# non-standard public port.

{$BACKEND_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy backend:8000
}
